**Definition 2.4 (actual legal requests and stopped successors).** The
original relative-command convention is [Probability/Phase Transport][PP]
§9.1. A public pair of relative increments $(a(t),b(t))$, starting at zero,
means $k(t)=x+a(t)$ and $\chi(t)=\chi_*+b(t)$. Its mathematical domain is
$(\ell_b-\min a,u_b-\max a)$, where $J_b=(\ell_b,u_b)$.
This partial operation is not a detector of unknown-domain violations.

Here the positive ramp of displacement $d>0$ and duration $L>0$ has domain
$(0,c-d)$. A positive return excursion of amplitude $d$ has the same
domain; its negative mirror has domain $(d,c)$. Each request below is
promised legal on its stated source catalogue, with common permissions.
Known permission denial or known mismatch has only its declared visible
unexecuted rejection and controller update. No executed successor is claimed
for a mathematically undefined request. A total unknown-height guard is an
additional target, used only as the decision consumer of §9.

For a separately supplied legal matching continuation, literal composition
uses $\chi(T+u)=\chi(T)+\chi_{\rm tail}(u)-\chi_{\rm tail}(0)$.
It neither reads nor resets the old lift. Zero duration permits the matching
zero-displacement identity; it permits no instantaneous nonzero leg.
First executed failure keeps its exact time, original mode and absorbing
$f$, with all old archives and updates. No later positive-carrier operation,
retry, reset, reversal or replacement specimen follows it.

